# Build output and demo scratch. `make clean` removes this directory.
# It holds the compiled binary, coverage reports, generated plan artifacts and
# the file state store the demo targets use.
build/

# Plan artifacts are environment-bound: the topology fingerprint ties one to a
# single database's catalog, so a plan built against staging is refused against
# production. What belongs in version control is the SPECIFICATION, the way you
# commit .tf and not .tfplan. See docs/HANDOFF.md P1.
*.plan

# Local configuration may carry a DSN.
partitionctl.yaml

.DS_Store

# Maven build output.
target/

# Internal working documents. These stay on the author's disk and out of the public
# repository. They record how the work was driven and reasoned about — handovers, planning,
# directives, adversarial review rounds, experiment write-ups, proof-of-concept harnesses and
# agent orchestration scripts. None is needed to build, run, adopt or contribute to either
# product; the conclusions that matter are stated in README.md and CLAUDE.md.
#
# Ignored, NOT deleted. Note that `git bundle` does not carry untracked files, so moving this
# checkout to another machine means copying docs/ across separately.

# Handover, planning and tracking
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/M4-HANDOFF.md
docs/M4-PLAN.md
docs/M2-M3-DIRECTIVE.md
docs/M2-M3-FOUNDATION.md
docs/REPAIR-REPORT.md
docs/REVIEW-ROUND1.md
docs/REVIEW-ROUND2.md
docs/NEW-MACHINE-PROMPT.md
docs/LAPTOP-TRANSFER.md
docs/TRD.md
docs/workflows/

# Experiment write-ups: the raw research record behind the measured facts.
docs/experiments/*.md

# Proof-of-concept harnesses, kept as evidence of how each phase was proven.
# m4-e2e is the exception and stays tracked: `make lb-e2e` executes it.
docs/experiments/poc-trees/README.md
docs/experiments/poc-trees/poc/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4-gate/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4-drop-gate/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4-preconditions/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4-reindex/
docs/experiments/poc-trees/m4-repair/

# Session tooling for Claude Code, not part of either product.
.claude/
